<title>BELGIUM: Belgian money market supply cut in week.</title>
<headline>Belgian money market supply cut in week.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian National Bank said on Wednesday it withdrew liquidity from the money market in the week to January 13, mainly by cutting the amount of repurchase agreements outstanding, following a decrease of bank notes in circulation and of Belgian state deposits.</p>
<p>(figures from the weekly statement in bln francs) -</p>
<p> Foreign currency reserves	   434.01 (+  2.51)</p>
<p> Advances against pledged security  16.39 (+  1.67)</p>
<p> Commercial bills			  3.15 (-  0.03)</p>
<p> Securities portfolio		   24.88 (-  0.01)</p>
<p> Money market interventions*	  99.32 (- 21.34)</p>
<p> Bank notes in circulation	   452.51 (-  8.43)</p>
<p>* comprises repurchase agreements and interbank loans</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
